{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Yehudah, you — your brothers shall praise you.</b> Since he rebuked the earlier ones with reproofs, Yehudah began to draw back behind him (lest he rebuke him over the matter of Tamar), so he called him with words of appeasement: Yehudah — you are not like them (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Your hand on the neck of your enemies.</b> In the days of David — ״וְאֹיְבַי תַּתָּה לִּי עֹרֶף״ (II Samuel 22)." "<b>Your father's sons.</b> Because they were from many women, he did not say 'your mother's sons,' as Yitzchak said."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:02.214291541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}